Task 2. Root Servers https://root-servers.org/
The DNS Root Servers are the highest level of servers in the Domain Name System (DNS) hierarchy. Their role is to help computers locate the correct DNS servers responsible for different domain names on the Internet.
A user enters the following address into a web browser: www.lmu.edu in a browser. 
•	Explain the role of the DNS root server in resolving the domain name 
The top in terms of DNS and power, direct the right DNS to the TLD servers
•	Describe the steps involved in the DNS lookup process, starting from the user's computer request until the IP address of the website is returned. 
•	enters www.lmu.edu in browser, computer checks local DNS, root server directs the resolver to the .edu TLD servers, TLD server provides info for authorization to the DNS server for the lmu.edu, resolver contacts authoritative DNS server to get the websites DNS record, resolver returns reolved IP to user, browser uses the IP to connect.

